    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/program-assistant-exercise-science-neuroscience-and-physics-astronomy-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Job Description for the Program Assistant",
      "description": "Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 University Administration Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: M-F Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience High School Diploma and minimum of 2 years of experience in an office or related environment. Job Duties Provide front office support to the Units represented Maintain the Unit's calendar/schedule, anticipate annual cycle of required meetings and reports across academic year and ensure that the Chair completes those items in a timely manner Maintain the faculty, staff, and department digital records (annual reports, assessment reports, and external reviews for the department) Maintain strict confidentiality related to personnel and student needs Assist faculty, as needed, in summarizing department level reports On board new faculty and staff within the Unit, including training and meetings with key offices Event planning and communication for Unit office(s) (e.g., faculty meetings, graduation events, etc.) Support University Communications liaison to the College in maintenance of the Unit webpages Reflects a unified voice of the College in the operations and communications with other offices on campus and throughout higher education. Train and supervise student workers within the Unit's office Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Apply now! Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/program-assistant-school-of-communications-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Assistant, School of Communications",
      "description": "Program Assistant, School of Communications - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Program Assistant, School of Communications position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Program Assistant, School of Communications Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 University Administration Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Program Assistant, School of Communications Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: School of Communications Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary Program Assistant, School of Communications The program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree required, with computer and software proficiency Job Duties Serve as the point of first contact for visitors to the School of Communications by greeting those who come to the office and answering the phone. Provide administrative support for the deans, chairs, faculty and staff. Schedule appointments for staff persons located in the student affairs office of McEwen (internship director, the director of student engagement and alumni affairs, and three Student Professional Development Center staff members assigned to communications). Assist faculty and staff with instructional supplies, copying and issues. Monitor and order office supplies and promotional materials. Serve as the McEwen building manager and coordinate with facilities management and IT to resolve maintenance issues. Schedule McEwen meeting spaces. Work with Admissions on prospective student visitors and special events such as Fellows Weekend. Lead all aspects of event planning for School of Communications events. Support student affairs, development and industry partnerships through accessing and updating relevant databases. Provide support for the Student Media Board and take minutes at the monthly meetings. Provide support for the Dean’s Student Advisory Board. Serve as backup to the administrative team in the dean’s office, providing logistical and administrative support as needed. Willingness to advise the Unity in Communications student organization is a plus. Manage travel itineraries for campus visitors, including booking flights, hotels, and rentals. Support School of Communications centers and grant-funded programs (including, but not limited to, the North Carolina Open Government Coalition and the Emerging Journalists Program) and Other duties as assigned. Please attach a Cover Letter to your application. Apply now! Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
