    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/adjunct-instructor-sport-management-department-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Adjunct Add to favorites View favorites Part-time instructors in Sport Management – Elon University JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. These appointments are part-time, non-tenure track, with no guarantee of renewal. Our classes will be in-person either M-W-F, for 70 minutes each class, or T-TH, for 100 minutes each class. We also have a few M-W afternoon classes, for 100 minutes each class. Courses include, but are not limited to: Sport Law, Sport & Media, Sport Communications, Research Methods, Event & Venue Management, Sport Marketing, Sport Promotion & Sales, and Sport Finance. A terminal degree in sport management or other closely related field is preferred. Candidates should have teaching experience, as well as professional experience in sport management industries/fields. Applicants must demonstrate a commitment to inclusive, student-centered teaching and clear, skills-based assessment.Applicants should apply by submitting a short letter of interest with their qualifications, current Curriculum Vita (CV) and contact information of at least three references. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and positions filled as needed. For information about Elon University’s Sport Management Department, please visit https://www.elon.edu/u/academics/communications/sport-management/ Elon University is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff and student body and welcomes all applicants. Apply now! Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
