    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/program-assistant-departments-of-computer-science-engineering-physics-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics",
      "description": "Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 University Administration Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: M-F Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: School of Engineering and Computing Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary The Program Assistant for the Departments of Computer Science, Engineering and Physics provides support to faculty, staff, and students within the three departments and coordinates day-to-day operations. This vital member of the Elon University School of Engineering & Computing interacts daily with students, faculty, and staff by providing clerical and office management support, by supervising student employees, and by providing written/oral communications to both internal and external audiences. The position also works closely with the Office of the Dean and other units across the University. To be successful in this position, the Program Assistant must possess the following qualities: • highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities • has a positive attitude that contributes to a collaborative culture • acts with flexibility and patience while remaining calm under pressure • willingness to learn new skills and programs • demonstrates good judgment and attention to detail • comfortable and confident working with students’ FERPA-protected information; • strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills • ability to work both independently and collaboratively, as part of a team on multiple projects simultaneously • proficiency with Microsoft products such as Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams, also able to learn internal University platforms Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience HS Diploma and 2-5 years of experience in an office setting Preferred Education and Experience Associate's Degree (AA) in a related field and/or experience in education support, non-profit administrative support, other related field, or a combination of education and experience Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A successful candidate will show evidence of: • ability to prioritize work according to departmental needs, can determine workflow problems and develop solutions, and efficiently execute workflows • proficiency with computer technology and Microsoft Office applications including Outlook, Teams, Word, and Excel • willingness/ability to learn new computer programs and software associated with administrative tasks at Elon • strong oral and written communication skills • professional and courteous manner and an ability to work harmoniously with other staff, faculty, students and other constituents. • exceptional time management and organizational skills • sharp attention to detail with the ability to multitask • regular attendance and punctuality • ability to independently plan, organize, and carry out work assignments • appropriate discretion when handling information that is both sensitive and confidential in nature Job Duties Administrative Support Collect, enter and update information in the university data systems Provide collaborative supervision for student staff members Support departmental hiring processes Plan and manage itineraries for interviewees, special guests, and other visitors Assist with the tracking and distribution of enrollment data Schedule room reservations as needed Participate as needed, in special department projects Attend and participate in staff development opportunities Communicate regularly with departmental faculty, particularly department chairs, to ensure timely handling of both regular and special departmental functions Communication & Event Support Assist with the planning and execution of departmental events Carefully prepare, review and edit various types of communications Assist with event and travel planning Financial Support Prepare check requests and purchase orders Assist in budget oversight, including monitor and reconcile expenses Manage procurement card expenses and allocations for the departments Process purchase, work, print, and catering orders; maintain financial records Community-Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Special Instructions to Applicants: Priority consideration will be given to applicants who have submitted their complete application, resume and 3 references with contact information on or before September 28, 2026. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 9df1ba75 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) c53c21b1 Last Name (required) e8c7c43b Email (required) 2bea79f0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the 