    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/financial-aid-customer-service-specialist-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist",
      "description": "Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Finance Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Admissions and Financial Aid Department: Financial Aid Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary This position serves as a primary customer service representative for the Office of Financial Aid. Primary duties will be the monitoring of the department email and fax accounts, answering telephones, working with students and parents in the front office and scanning, indexing, and maintaining the document imaging system. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Associate degree, or vocational or technical school degree in any relevant field of study with minimum 1 year of experience with the following relevant work experience: Administrative support experience involving data entry, document collection, record maintenance, and use of computerized information systems such as MS Office. Preferred Education and Experience Associate degree, vocational certificate, or technical school credential in a related field of study. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong communication skills (both oral and written) to include appropriate tone, clarity, and timeliness. Willingness to learn and the ability to adapt to an ever-changing working environment. Exhibits a commitment to inclusive excellence through interactions with colleagues, students, and visitors. Job Duties Customer Service Monitoring and answering of FinAid email, FinFax transmissions, and FinAid Check Teams Group. Answering incoming telephone calls from students and parents. Assisting students and parents in the office. Answers questions regarding FAFSA filing, loan applications, adjustments to aid, requests for adjustment, verification, requested documents, etc. General Office Duties Scanning and indexing of important student documents into document imaging system and general maintenance and organization of system. Assisting with processes within the office as needed Office Support Assisting with training and development of student employees. Support all Admissions events as needed for our department. Other duties as assigned. Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert a6ae73e0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Financial Aid Financial Aid Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 208d0f52 Last Name (required) a0c22691 Email (required) 2e857bab Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 10ee24bb Last Name (required) 8d629048 Email (required) cc8e24f6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/fleet-mechanic-ii-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states-1950401d-dded-4cd4-a8f6-d240c91ffeba": {
      "title": "Job Description for the Fleet Mechanic II position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position.",
      "description": "Fleet Mechanic II - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Fleet Mechanic II position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Fleet Mechanic II Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Facilities Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Fleet Mechanic II Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Finance and Administration Department: Facilities Management Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary Responsible for performing a variety of maintenance and/or repair tasks in a repair shop or in the field as assigned by a Fleet Mechanic I or Automotive Supervisor. Work is of average difficulty and is performed on automotive, transit fleet vehicles, and/or special vehicles and equipment that are gasoline, diesel and/or propane powered, with varying degrees of supervision based upon aptitude and skills required. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience High school diploma or GED with minimum 3 years of experience Preferred Education and Experience Associate degree, or vocational or technical school degree in Automotive Technology Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Use of automotive diagnostic monitors, and automotive maintenance software desirable. Job Duties Car/small vehicle repair Under general supervision perform and/or assist with major mechanical repairs such as transmission and engine rebuild on university vehicles and equipment Perform complete brake jobs on cars and medium duty trucks. Perform minor mechanical repairs on small engines and equipment such as water pumps, fuel pumps and alternators. Scheduled Maintenance Repair, mount, balance and install tires Complete Preventative Maintenance checks and repairs. Wash vehicles. Pick up and deliver vehicles and parts. Miscellaneous projects Perform shop housekeeping duties maintaining a safe work environment Conduct installation and removal of auxiliary equipment such as police radios and other equipment in university police vehicles. Make welding repairs and fabricate small metal projects. Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Special Instructions to Applicants: Rotation 24/7 on call every 6 weeks for a 2-week period. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 84ca7880 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Management Facilities Management Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 80679547 Last Name (required) 462d3995 Email (required) 119cc3f2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 10fc8e6b Last Name (required) 9dba4cf9 Email (required) 8c7d52d5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
