    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/associate-vice-president-for-student-professional-development-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development",
      "description": "Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Advancement Services Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Generally Monday through Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: University Advancement Department: Student Professional Development Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary The Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development is a senior leader responsible for advancing the university’s mission through building, scaling, and sustaining high-impact employer partnerships that drive internships, experiential learning, and full-time employment outcomes for students and alumni. This position provides strategic vision and executive oversight for all career services functions, with a focus on employer engagement, relationship management, workforce alignment, and student career outcomes. The Associate Vice President is a builder who will serve as Elon’s chief architect of employer strategy, developing innovative, scalable partnerships that align academic programs with workforce needs, expanding meaningful experiential learning opportunities, and strengthening postgraduate employment success. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience KEY COMPETENCIES Relationship-building and business development Strategic, student-centered thinking Deep understanding of workforce trends and the recruiting landscape Inspired collaboration Systems orientation Management of multiple priorities in a highly-complex environment Cultural fluency Executive communication Commitment to excellence Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree required; Advanced degree preferred 10-15 years of significant leadership and progressive accomplishments in complex environments Demonstrated excellence in: Building best-in-class organizational relationships Recruiting, inspiring, and leading teams Developing strategy and animating action Driving measurable outcomes Job Duties STRATEGIC LEADERSHIP Position Elon as a premier talent partner for regional, national, and global employers. Develop and execute a comprehensive, data-driven employer engagement strategy aligned with the university’s strategic plan and centering on excellence in student outcomes. Build deep, long-term partnerships with employers by assembling a team that is externally focused Establish and deliver upon measurable, meaningful goals related to employer partnerships, internships, job placement, and career outcomes. Advise senior leadership on workforce trends, industry alignment, and career success metrics EMPLOYER AND INDUSTRY PARTNERSHIPS Build and sustain executive-level relationships with employers across key industry sectors. Leverage Elon’s alumni, parent, and donor networks to expand partnerships that generate internships, co-ops, research collaborations, on-campus recruiting, and full-time employment pipelines. Lead corporate outreach efforts, including targeted industry engagement strategies and employer advisory boards. Collaborate with campus partners to align employer engagement with corporate sponsorships and philanthropic opportunities. Promote equitable access to opportunities through diverse and inclusive employer partnerships. WORKFORCE ALIGNMENT Partner with academic leadership to align curricula with evolving industry needs. Identify emerging workforce trends and translate insights into programmatic opportunities. Develop sector-based career pathways and employer pipelines in high-growth fields. Facilitate employer input into curriculum design, credentialing, and experiential learning. OUTCOMES AND ASSESSMENT Establish and monitor KPIs related to job placement, internship participation, employer satisfaction, and graduate outcomes. Lead post-graduation outcomes reporting and ensure compliance with accreditation and regulatory standards. Use data analytics to drive continuous improvement and strategic decision-making. MANAGEMENT AND VISIONING Lead inspired planning aligned with the university’s strategic plan, Boldly Elon. Manage a team of 30 across three campuses, including six direct reports, fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration, and precision in execution. EXTERNAL REPRESENTATION Represent Elon at industry forums, workforce development boards, chambers of commerce, and other venues that elevate the university’s brand. Partner with the Office of Admissions to champion career outcomes for prospective students and families. Special Instructions to Applicants: ** This search is being conducted by The Duffy Group. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, current resume, and three references saved as one document, either Word or a PDF. The file name should start with your first name and then last name, such as, “John Doe - Elon Application.” This should be emailed to lpas@duffygroup.com with the email subject of “Application for Elon AVP.” Applications received through the Elon system will not be reviewed by the search firm. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1b409fd8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 9e975b5e Last Name (required) 849aa2bd Email (required) 4abbaf35 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Heal