    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/botanical-garden-coordinator-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Botanical Garden Coordinator",
      "description": "Botanical Garden Coordinator - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Botanical Garden Coordinator position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Botanical Garden Coordinator Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Facilities Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Botanical Garden Coordinator Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Finance and Administration Department: Facilities Management Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary The Botanical Garden Coordinator is responsible for the health and appearance of the campus botanical gardens and landscape. The primary responsibilities include overall responsibility for the appearance of gardens, overseeing the design of display beds, coordinating planting and maintaining annual floral display beds, garden expansion, improvement of garden areas, acquisition of plants and materials, and landscape renovation. Other responsibilities include assisting with garden visits, marketing of the gardens, updating the gardens web pages, perennial and shrub gardens maintenance to include; mulch beds, pruning, weed control. The Botanical Garden Coordinator may be assigned other tasks or projects by the Director of Landscaping. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Associate degree, or vocational or technical school degree in Horticulture, landscape design, landscape management, or related field. with more than 8 years of experience with the following relevant work experience: A four-year bachelor's degree in Horticulture, landscape design, or related field, plus a minimum of eight (8) years' work experience in horticulture or related field; or a two year associated degree in Horticulture, landscape design, or related field plus ten (10) years' work experience in horticulture is required. Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor's degree in Horticulture, landscape design, landscape management, or related field. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES This position has no formal supervisory responsibilities. However, the Botanical Garden Coordinator will take the lead on projects, when working on projects, they will prioritize tasks and delegate those tasks associated with the project to assigned staff. LANGUAGE SKILLS Must have the ability to read, analyze and interpret professional journals and technical literature. Verbal skills required to effectively communicate work assignments and interacting with landscape contractors. MATHMATICS SKILLS Must be able to understand basic arithmetic calculations in order to calculate areas, calibrate application equipment and apply fertilizers and pesticides accurately. Able to perform accurate materials and cost estimates for projects. REASONING ABILITY Must be able to perform detailed visual observation of plants and gardens and ascertain information, while working in the field, to determine if there is a general decline in the health of plant material and determine what corrective measures must be taken. OTHER SKILLS REQUIRED Computer experience with PC's, experience with Microsoft Office applications including Word and Excel is required. Landscape design skill, experience and demonstrated ability. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to organize, motivate and lead a diverse group are required. Success is based on the ability to work with an extremely broad social and intellectual assortment of people. Able to identify the majority of landscape plants on the Elon Campus and demonstrate a thorough knowledge of their cultural requirements. Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing CERTIFICATES OR LICENSES Must possess a valid NC Driver's license and be insurable by the University carrier. A NC Pesticide License is required, or must be obtained within six months of employment. A NC Plant Professional Certification is required, or must be obtained within six months of employment. Job Duties Responsible for managing the health and appearance of designated botanical garden collections and landscaped areas on campus. This shall include: Diagnosing plant health issues or improper growing conditions; following appropriate IPM practices to determine and direct pesticide applications, weed control and fertilization; and directing watering, pruning and removal of plant material. Perform and/or oversee the planning, designing, acquiring, and coordinating seasonal display beds. Changes in accordance with the seasonal calendar, the university calendar, special events, and weather conditions to assure the desired level of quality, appearance, cleanliness, and plant health. Responsible for enhancing and improving the existing and new campus landscaped spaces. To include, but not limited to, annual/bi-annual plant replacements across campus and procurement of plants and materials within allocated resources. This will include design and input of plant and materials for new landscaped areas. Coordinate installation of the plant replacements. Oversee the planning and designing of the expansion of the campus botanical gardens. Continue and expand initiatives to expand collections, gardens, and the communication of relevant information to students, faculty, and visitors. Will assist with campus garden visits, updating of plant collection lists, and marketing of the university botanical gardens. Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Special Instructions to Applicants: The position is part of the Elon Emergency Response team and is required to be available to assist with preparation, throughout, and after inclement weather events. This is not limited to only inclement weather events, but all University emergency events. There is evenings and weekend work from time to time. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 88ab7d8c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Management Facilities Management Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 30cbcc9d Last Name (required) ea81f1d5 Email (required) 3d40d3f5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) e24e1673 Last Name (required) 038ec345 Email (required) 14ce02d3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/department-of-physical-therapy-education-faculty-member-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states-6c00c796-53e5-4b1d-bf20-8f0b63971940": {
      "title": "Job Description for the Department of Physical Therapy Education Faculty Member position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position.",
      "description": "Department of Physical Therapy Education Faculty Member - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Department of Physical Therapy Education Faculty Member position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Department of Physical Therapy Education Faculty Member Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Faculty Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites DPTE Faculty Search Announcement 2026 The Elon University Department of Physical Therapy Education and the School of Health Sciences announce the availability of two full-time tenure-track or continuing track positions at the Associate or Assistant Professor level to join a dynamic, private, in-person institution with a national model recognized for actively engaging students and faculty in teaching and learning. Due to retirements, we invite applications for two full-time, tenure or continuing track faculty positions at the Associate or Assistant Professor level. The department of 14 full-time and 6 part-time highly qualified, dynamic faculty is interested in recruiting individuals with demonstrated excellent teaching and clinical experience, preferably in Anatomical Sciences or Musculoskeletal physical therapy practice, directing the Elon Sports Physical Therapy Residency, and other courses based on departmental need and areas of expertise. Candidates with experience in prosthetics and orthotics, integumentary, clinical reasoning, and clinical imaging will also be considered. Experience with post-professional mentoring is preferred. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, student mentoring, and service to the department, school, and university. The successful candidate will have effective interpersonal and communication skills, as well as a commitment to collaborative teamwork and professional growth. The start date for these positions is negotiable. Successful candidates will have: A record of excellent teaching and ongoing scholarship related to physical therapy practice, education, or rehabilitation/movement science Eligibility for licensure as a physical therapist in North Carolina A minimum of 3 years of clinical practice Active membership in the APTA A DPT degree from an accredited institution ABPTS Board Certification or an academic terminal degree (e.g., PhD, EdD, DSc). Preferred candidates will have: Experience as a mid-career content specialist and mentor An academic terminal degree (Candidates who are in the dissertation candidacy phase will be considered) Active participation or mentorship in a professional organization Commitment to inclusive professional and educational practices Clinical, educational, or mentorship experience in residency or fellowship for the Musculoskeletal position Evidence of engaged teaching practices including experience with donor-based Anatomy instruction for the Anatomical Sciences position About Elon University: Elon University is a mid-sized private university located in central North Carolina, renowned nationally as a model for engaged and experiential learning. The university is recognized as one of the nation's most beautiful collegiate environments and a place where students work closely with faculty who are teacher-scholar-mentors. The undergraduate curriculum is grounded in the traditional liberal arts and sciences and complemented by nationally accredited professional and graduate programs. With a focus on teaching and student success, Elon was honored to be ranked among the top universities in the nation by US News & World Report, receiving a #1 ranking for excellence in undergraduate teaching and a #10 ranking for \"Best-Run\" Colleges. The University comprises six schools with a selective student body of over 7,000. Elon is one of only seven private universities in the country with accredited schools of business, communications, education, law, and health sciences, plus a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, the nation's oldest and most prestigious academic honor society. About the School of Health Sciences: The School of Health Sciences was established in 2011 and includes graduate programs in Physical Therapy, Physician Assistant Studies and Clinical Mental Health Counseling in addition to the four-year Bachelor of Science in Nursing and Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing. The school and its programs are dedicated to innovative educational programming, engaged and distinctive healthcare education, an inclusive and supportive community for working and learning, regional health partnerships, and lifelong learning and professional development. The School of Health Sciences is located in the LEED-certified Gerald L. Francis Center, a state-of-the-art teaching and research facility. Faculty, staff, and students in all programs collaborate on innovative research initiatives in interdisciplinary laboratories, including the biomechanics lab. Our Interprofessional Simulation Center is a hub of experiential learning, allowing students to hone their skills in providing individualized care at the bedside, in the clinic, in the home, and in the community. Elon’s Anatomical Gift Program provides a meaningful way to contribute to the healthcare education of enrolled Physical Therapy and Physician Assistant students and full curricular support with access to first-person consenting human donors. About the Department of Physical Therapy Education: The Department of Physical Therapy Education (DPTE) enjoys a strong collaborative partnership with nearby Cone Health-Alamance Regional Medical Center. The Department includes an accredited Sports Physical Therapy Residency with a Division 1 athletic setting, opportunities for global learning, and a dedicated student research coordinator. The DPTE occupies approximately 32,000 square feet with equipment for teaching and research, such as MSK ultrasound, DEXA scanner, strength and balance measuring systems, a markerless 3D motion capture system which includes 12 cameras and a 16-channel wireless EMG system, two force plates for gait analysis, a Woodway Pro-Treadmill, instrumented walkways, a body-weight support rehabilitation system, and a Galileo whole-body vibration training device. The DPTE houses the Health Outreach Program of Elon (HOPE Clinic). Serving patients since 2013, the HOPE Clinic is a student-managed pro bono clinic offering free physical therapy services to those who are uninsured or underinsured in Alamance County and surrounding areas. Please visit our website at www.elon.edu/dpt for additional information about the DPTE. Elon is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body, and welcomes all applicants. Application Process: Correspondence relating to the positions should be directed in confidence to the Search Committee Co-Chairs: Alys Giordano, Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Education: agiordano4@elon.edu Jack Magill, Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Education: jmagill@elon.edu A complete application through PageUP should include: Updated CV Letter of Intent: Outlining your interest and qualifications for the position Teaching philosophy Research statement/anticipated agenda Three professional references (references will not be contacted until after first interview) Applications received by September 5, 2026, will receive priority consideration. The search will remain open until the positions are filled. Salary and rank will be commensurate with qualifications and level of experience. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ed36cde4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Health Sciences School of Health Sciences Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 6158cb28 Last Name (required) c7c77391 Email (required) 3c0e4d8e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. Project Manager, Integration President's Office The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) a749407f Last Name (required) 2bfa0a72 Email (required) bd2e55ec Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
