    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/3rd-shift-floor-tech-sunday-thursday-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Job Description for the 3rd shift Floor Tech Sunday-Thursday position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position.",
      "description": "3rd shift Floor Tech Sunday-Thursday - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the 3rd shift Floor Tech Sunday-Thursday position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. 3rd shift Floor Tech Sunday-Thursday Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Facilities Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: 3rd shift Floor Tech Sunday-Thursday Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Sunday-Thursday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Finance and Administration Department: Facilities Management Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary The floor technician position is responsible for helping to maintain a clean and safe environment for the Elon University Campus. This includes, but not limited to, custodial duties, maintaining and cleaning equipment, vacuuming, sweeping, and mopping floors, and the stripping, sealing, finishing of floors, carpet cleaning and upholstery cleaning. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience High school diploma or GED with less than 1 year of experience Preferred Education and Experience High school diploma or GED Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to use your abdominal and lower back muscles to support part of the body repeatedly or continuously over time without ‘giving out' or fatiguing during cleaning. • The ability to bend, stretch, twist, or reach with your body, arms, and/or legs. • Ability to inspect equipment, structures, or materials to identify the cause of errors or other problems or defects. • Ability to communicate information to supervisors or co-workers by telephone or in person. • Ability to operate vacuums and other related equipment. Job Duties Maintain Cleanliness of Campus Clean all areas of the assigned building. Follow procedures for the use of chemical cleaners and power equipment to prevent damage to floors and fixtures. Short list of cleaning duties are as follows: Strip, seal and finish all hard floor surfaces. Clean carpets and upholstery, Mop, sweep, and vacuum floors daily. Sweep all stairwells and landings and complete daily tasks assigned by shift supervisor. Clean and sanitize areas that may contain biohazardous materials/fluids. Assist and perform other duties as assigned including but not limited to snow removal and storm damage recovery. Stock Cleaning Cabinets Maintain floor maintenance worker closets in a neat and orderly fashion. Requisition supplies or equipment needed for cleaning and maintenance duties. Maintain Cleaning Equipment Maintain and clean all floor equipment reporting mechanical problems to the shift supervisor for proper repairs. Reporting Maintenance Issues Found on Campus Notify the proper channels with repairs to heating, cooling, ventilating, plumbing, or electrical systems are needed. Building Safety and Security Use of wet floor signs, bathroom cleaning signs, and other safety signs when appropriate Annual Training Perform other duties deemed necessary by the shift supervisor. Attend and utilize information provided by yearly training. Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 05d00555 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Management Facilities Management Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 412c053b Last Name (required) 7ee54a6c Email (required) 3f5c119d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies School of Health Sciences Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments.\n\nClinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department School of Communications The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon'